// A capture with no closing brace — a common typo, and the one that makes a
// backtick template non-terminating: under D10 a backtick inside a capture
// opens a template of its own, so the second backtick here is an opener and the
// run never closes.
//
// The lexer's `T002` is the truthful report. What must NOT also appear is a
// second diagnostic about the *interior*: there is no interior to scan, and the
// predecessor manufactured one out of the whole token and reported "unterminated
// nested template" — a construct this file does not contain — at a byte offset
// that means nothing.
